{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of upward momentum: The model fails to capture rapid price spikes (e.g., 68 to 80 EUR), consistently forecasting flat or slightly rising trends while true outcomes surge. Apply a positive momentum adjustment when recent history shows a sharp upward inflection.",
    "Implement aggressive mean reversion after peaks: The model exhibits a 'lag' in recognizing trend reversals, continuing to forecast higher prices immediately after a peak (e.g., 80.24) while true prices drop sharply. Reduce forecasts significantly in the 5-10 day horizon following a local maximum.",
    "Adjust for sentiment signal latency: Positive sentiment spikes (values > 0.20) often precede immediate price rallies that the model misses. Increase short-term forecasts (1-5 days) when sentiment history transitions from 0 to positive, even if the price trend appears flat.",
    "Reduce long-term forecast bias: The model systematically overestimates the floor price during downtrends (e.g., forecasting 69+ while prices fall to 61). Apply a downward drift correction to the tail of the 30-day forecast when the 18-day history shows a declining trend.",
    "Account for volatility clustering: The model assumes low volatility (smooth curves) regardless of recent price swings. Introduce a volatility buffer to widen forecast ranges during periods of high historical variance."
  ]
}
